    "open_questions": [
      "The Drum Also Waltzes: Drumeo's transcription lists 81 bpm without saying which note; read the transcription (or the record) to settle whether it is the quarter or the dotted half.",
      "Garvey's Ghost (Percussion Bitter Sweet, 1961): Bishop has him playing 'a jazz waltz behind the 6/4 Afro feel' and Nasheet Waits hears him 'in 6 but also in 3'. Read Bishop's transcription to see whether that is a 2:3 hemiola against the vamp before tagging one.",
      "Un Poco Loco (Bud Powell, 1951): the cowbell figure is '5 over the 4' (Waits), 'whole note triplets across the barline' (Boudreau) and 'at a different tempo' on the bass drum (Kaplan). Find a transcription that settles it.",
      "Jazz in 3/4 Time: no source read names a hemiola in his own part on the waltzes; read Francis's Blues Waltz transcription.",
      "Read Bishop's PDFs (Blue Seven, Minor Meeting, A Little Sweet, Freedom Suite) for the bars themselves; the songs here follow his prose.",
      "Freedom Suite (Rollins, 1958): the rubadub is described, but no tempo was found.",
      "As Long As You're Living (Quiet As It's Kept): a blues in 5/4 at 186 (Bishop); how he splits the five is not described."
    ]
  },
